screens.prose:
Each Python special method has a C++ operator: `__add__` is `operator+`, `__eq__` is `operator==`, `__lt__` is `operator<`, and `__repr__` becomes `operator<<`. The usual shapes:

```cpp
Money operator+(Money a, Money b);       // new value
Money operator*(Money m, int k);         // by value
Money operator*(int k, Money m);         // other order
Money& operator+=(Money& a, Money b);    // mutates
bool operator==(const Money&, const Money&);
bool operator<(const Money&, const Money&);
std::ostream& operator<<(std::ostream&, const Money&);
```

